# Canonical Lib Modules — VTC Apps

Auth flow: `auth-bootstrap.mdc`. JWT claims: `auth-jwt-reference.mdc`.

## `jwt.ts`

```typescript
export type AuthenticatedUser = { /* see auth-jwt-reference.mdc */ }
export function decodeJwt(token: string): AuthenticatedUser | null
export function getTokenFromRequest(request: Request): string | null
```

Reject expired tokens. Validate URL `user` === `user_id` and URL `group` === `group_id`.

`decodeJwt` is for display only (names, role badges in the browser). It does not check the
signature, so it must never decide access on the server.

## `auth.ts`

```typescript
// Server only. Confirms the token with the VTC API before trusting any claim.
export async function getAuthenticatedUser(request: NextRequest): Promise<AuthenticatedUser | null>
export function isOwner(user: AuthenticatedUser): boolean   // role_type === "1"
export function isAdmin(user: AuthenticatedUser): boolean    // role_type "1" or "2"
```

Implement it with `@vtc/auth`: `getAuthenticatedUser(request, { requireVerified: true })`
(GET `/api/v1/auth/verify` with the Bearer token, cached briefly). Always `await` it — an
un-awaited call is a Promise, so `if (!user)` would let every request through. Details:
`auth-jwt-reference.mdc` → Server verification.

## `clientAuth.ts`

Required exports — full signatures in `auth-bootstrap.mdc`. Accent persistence: `ui.mdc`.

```typescript
const TOKEN_KEY = 'posif_token'
const MODE_KEY = 'posif_mode'
const COLOR_KEY = 'posif_color'
const LANG_KEY = 'posif_lang'

export function bootstrapAuthFromUrl(): void
export function preserveThemeParams(): void
export function getPersistedThemeParams(): { mode?: string; color?: string; lang?: string }
export function getAuthToken(): string | null
export function addTokenToUrl(url: string): string
```

| Function | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `bootstrapAuthFromUrl` | URL → `posif_token`, `posif_user`, `posif_group` |
| `preserveThemeParams` | URL `mode` / `color` / `lang` → `posif_mode` / `posif_color` / `posif_lang` |
| `getPersistedThemeParams` | Read theme keys when query params are stripped |
| `addTokenToUrl` | Re-append `token`, `user`, `group`, `mode`, `color`, `lang` (URL or persisted) |

**Also required:** `src/lib/accent.ts` (or `accentColor.ts`) with `resolveAccentColor()` — handles `#hex`, bare hex, and named colors (`green`, `blue`, …). Reference: `~/apps/lists`.

**Do not** ship a `clientAuth.ts` that only appends `token` (or `token` + `lang`) — space accent will not survive token strip or in-app navigation.

## `mongodb.ts`

```typescript
export function connectDB(user: AuthenticatedUser): Promise<Db>
// MONGODB_DEV_URI (localhost) in dev; MONGODB_URI in production
```

## `db.ts`

```typescript
export async function getDbWithAuth(request: NextRequest): Promise<{ db: Db; user: AuthenticatedUser }>
export async function getDbOptionalAuth(request: NextRequest): Promise<{ db: Db | null; user: AuthenticatedUser | null }>
```

Shared vs Dedicated branching — `architecture.mdc`.

When the app declares **Personal** (`app-types.mdc`):

```typescript
export function getPersonalStore(request: NextRequest): {
  store: ReturnType<typeof personalDb>
  user: AuthenticatedUser
  token: string
}
```

Use `personalDb(request)` from `@vtc/sdk` ≥ 1.4.0 — **not** `getPersonalDb()`. Details: `personal-storage.mdc`.

